quran[6]{c,v,t}:
  4,135,"O Believers! Be maintainers of justice and be witnesses for the sake of Allah, even if it is against yourselves, or (your) parents and near relatives. Whether the person is rich or poor, Allah is nearer to both. Do not follow (your) desires lest you become unjust. And if you distort (the testimony) or decline (to give it), Allah is indeed All-Aware of what you do."
  4,136,"O believers! Believe in Allah, His Messenger (blessings and peace be upon him), the Book He has revealed to His Messenger (blessings and peace be upon him) and the Book He has revealed before. Whoever disbelieves in Allah, His angels, His Books, His messengers, and the Last Day has surely strayed far into error."
  4,137,"Indeed, those who believe and then disbelieve, then believe and then disbelieve (again), and then increase in disbelief, Allah shall never forgive them, nor guide them to the (right) path."
  4,138,Inform the hypocrites that there is a painful punishment for them.
  4,139,"Those who ally themselves with the (hostile) disbelievers instead of the believers, do they seek honour (or power) through them? But all honour (and power) belongs to Allah."
  4,140,"Indeed, He has already revealed to you in the Book that when you hear Allah’s revelations being disbelieved and ridiculed, do not sit with them until they engage in some other discourse. Otherwise, you will then become like them. Indeed, Allah will gather the hypocrites and the disbelievers all together in Hell."
